# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# CFF has no field for contributors; the advisors of the thesis are listed as
# contributors with the role "Supervisor" in .zenodo.json.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the thesis."
title: "Conservative Crank–Nicolson–Ortigueira–Picard finite-difference solver for the fractional generalized Davey–Stewartson system"
abstract: >-
  Reference Python implementation and reproducibility package of the PhD thesis
  "Theoretical and Numerical Analysis of the Fractional Davey–Stewartson System"
  (Universidad de Guadalajara, 2026). A conservative Crank–Nicolson
  finite-difference scheme for the fractional generalized Davey–Stewartson
  system (FGDSS), with Ortigueira centered differences for the Riesz operators
  and a Picard iteration for the nonlinear coupling, together with the
  experiment drivers, tests, and archived results of every figure and table of
  Chapter 5 of the thesis.
